			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance with Cocoon and Wind IPC contract updates\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit 77ab17dd, incorporating critical architectural refinements from the Cocoon and Wind submodules to strengthen the gRPC and Tauri IPC boundaries.\n\nThe Cocoon update (bf9d9ffa) introduces `Types.ts` under `Source/Services/Mountain/gRPC` to formalize the contract between the extension host and native backend. It defines strict DTOs (e.g., `ShowTextDocumentOptions`, `TextEdit`) and the `IMountainGRPCClientService` interface, enabling strong typing for native operations without importing the full Effect-TS runtime.\n\nThe Wind update (a25a3c5b) adds `MountainCommands.ts` and `Converters.ts` to centralize file-system IPC method strings (e.g., `file:stat`, `file:readdir`) and implement pure conversion logic between VS Code URI shapes and Mountain's raw JSON responses. This isolates protocol mapping from core services, facilitating unit testing and ensuring synchronization with native handlers.\n\nThese changes enforce separation of concerns and type safety across the editor stack as the IPC architecture matures.",
			"SHA": "6c3de8c28bf007f6c0bcbb420dec0c6f3423c44e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:34:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance Cocoon formatting and Mountain dashboard helpers\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit e56eef10, incorporating refinements from the Cocoon and Mountain submodules.\n\nThe Cocoon update (8c25ad5a) standardizes the `UriKey` utility by formatting the `fsPath` conditional return statement, improving code consistency without altering logic. The Mountain update (e4c272b2) introduces `DashboardHelpers` under the `PerformanceDashboard` IPC module, adding stub utilities for process memory, CPU usage, and UUID generation, alongside a helper to map metric types to display strings.\n\nThese changes align the extension host and native backend with project coding standards and establish the foundational layer for future performance monitoring integration.\n\nRefs e56eef10595c5b6ed53e39aacc7a77a6cfef7b23",
			"SHA": "d9c579f246e0a633391f00fcd4d3f785271bec6f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:31:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance Cocoon with Language and Window API handlers\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit b1de8927, incorporating critical bridges between the Cocoon extension host and the Mountain native backend.\n\nThis update introduces the `RegisterProvider` mechanism to create auto-assigned handles, notify Mountain via gRPC (`Context.SendToMountain`), and return disposables for VS Code-compliant Language Providers. It adds `UriKey` for URI normalization to prevent diagnostic collisions and `MakeEventSubscriber` to standardize `this` binding for Window events. Furthermore, central Map registries are established for Tree Data, Webview View, and Custom Editor providers to ensure efficient O(1) lookups and state synchronization.\n\nThese changes enable the extension host to fully manage providers and events, completing the IPC bridge required for VS Code extension compatibility within the Land architecture.",
			"SHA": "0db33f4eceac14fbecd0e83c2620b4c55ab10159"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:29:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance to Wind IPC primitives and tracing utilities\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit 4d997a51, incorporating the latest changes from the Wind service layer.\n\nThis update introduces `MountainInvoke.ts` to encapsulate raw Tauri invocation logic (`InvokeMountain`, `InvokeViaNode`), centralizing native backend communication for the Wind architecture. Additionally, `Trace.ts` is added to provide non-invasive diagnostic tools (`Trace`, `DevLogForward`, `TimedTrace`) for OTEL performance collection and log mirroring to `Mountain.dev.log`.\n\nThese changes eliminate code duplication in the routing layer and establish a standardized observability surface, enabling structured error handling and performance monitoring across the editor's service layer.",
			"SHA": "b1213928406a3bce52a7c77e65b35176f136555d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:28:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Update submodule with Wind IPC routing and stub channels\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to commit 989e00d0, which incorporates updates from the Wind service layer.\n\nThe update introduces `ChannelRouteMap` to translate VS Code IPC channel names into Mountain `method:` prefixes, ensuring `TauriChannel.call` correctly dispatches requests to the native backend. It also establishes `StubChannels` to provide safe, typed default responses for unimplemented shared-process channels (e.g., sync, telemetry, webviews).\n\nThese changes prevent `Unknown method` runtime errors and undefined crashes by intercepting unimplemented IPC calls and returning plausible empty states, ensuring UI stability while native handlers are progressively implemented across the editor architecture.",
			"SHA": "ea1a2c1df38a5077df082cfbaa9473f5e3b8b93a"
		}
